From a238274c57330e4d1e7630478a8f9ba5f0786acb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:16:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel: material properties on the primitives of
 the backends shared with the behaviours

The generated code of a material property wrote, for each backend, the
whole evaluation of a batch (checks, statistics, kernels with and without
strides, merge of the statuses, stack size, launch, synchronization), with
its own hierarchy of backends. The behaviours and the models already called
a runtime and one primitive per backend: the middle layer of each backend
existed twice. The material properties now follow the same architecture:

- MFront/GenericParallel/<backend>.hxx: one primitive per backend (apply,
  makeApply), shared by the material properties, the behaviours and the
  models. It takes a handler of the statistics given by the interface.
  MFront/GenericParallel/Batch.hxx holds what is shared by the interfaces
  and the primitives: statistics of a batch, execution, report and
  handling of the exceptions (errno is now restored for the behaviours
  too). The headers of MFront/GenericParallelBehaviour only keep the
  functions specific to the behaviours (copies of the shared data, SYCL
  transfers).
- MFront/GenericParallelMaterialProperty/Evaluate.hxx: runtime of the
  material properties, counterpart of Integrate.hxx (checks of the batch,
  evaluation at the points, report by the generated report function).
  GenericParallelMaterialProperty/SYCL.hxx: transfers of the fields.
- The generated code of a material property only provides its evaluation
  at one point, its report function and a function of batches of the same
  form as the ones of the behaviours: about 210 lines for Inconel600, 486
  before with the arcane backend.
- One hierarchy of generators of backends for the three interfaces
  (MFront/GenericParallel/<name>Backend.hxx, namespace
  mfront::generic_parallel), told the runtime of the interface
  (AbstractBackend::Runtime). The hierarchy of the material properties is
  removed.
- The kernel specialized for unit strides is removed: no measurable gain
  (2^24 points, stlpar and openmp on 8 cores, CUDA on an RTX 5080), the
  evaluation being limited by the memory bandwidth.
- As for the behaviours, invalid parameters (-6) are reported before the
  other checks of a batch, and the execution policy is checked by the
  primitive. The error of the grid of a GPU gives the number of points for
  the behaviours too.

The data structures and the functions of the generated libraries are
unchanged.
