 of the backend. The options shared by the backends of both interfaces have
 the same meaning.
 
-The implementation differs. The code of a material property is a function
-of its arguments: the backends of the interface for material properties
-write a loop over the points in the generated code. The integration of a
-behaviour involves many more steps (gathering the data of a point, choice
-of the tangent operator, finite strain kinematics, statistics of the
-batch): the backends of the interface for behaviours call function
-templates, defined in the `MFront/GenericParallelBehaviour` headers, which
-only differ by the primitive applying a function at each point.
+The implementation is also shared. The generated functions call function
+templates of the runtime of their interface:
+`MFront/GenericParallelBehaviour/Integrate.hxx` for the behaviours and the
+models, `MFront/GenericParallelMaterialProperty/Evaluate.hxx` for the
+material properties. These templates check the batch and call the
+primitive of the backend, declared in `MFront/GenericParallel/<backend>.hxx`
+and shared by the three interfaces: it applies a function at each point and
+merges the statistics of the points. The generated code of a behaviour
+describes the data of a point and its integration, the one of a material
+property its evaluation at one point.
 
 Integrating a batch is equivalent to calling the function generated by the
 [`generic` interface](generic-behaviours-interface.html) at each
diff --git a/docs/web/generic-parallel-material-property-interface.md b/docs/web/generic-parallel-material-property-interface.md
index 4b8b8e587..4636c8543 100644
--- a/docs/web/generic-parallel-material-property-interface.md
+++ b/docs/web/generic-parallel-material-property-interface.md
@@ -138,8 +138,21 @@ An empty batch is accepted without any check, as an empty batch by the
 behaviours: nothing is read, written or submitted, and the status is
 `0`. The arrays and the execution policy may then be null.
 
-All the backends treat a batch of one point, and the case where all the
-strides are equal to one, with a kernel without strides.
+The strides are read at runtime by a single kernel, as for the
+behaviours. A kernel specialized for unit strides brought no measurable
+gain (\(2^{24}\) points, on the cores of the host and on a GPU): the
+evaluation of a material property is limited by the memory bandwidth.
+
+The generated code only provides the evaluation of the material property
+at one point. The runtime of the material properties
+(`MFront/GenericParallelMaterialProperty/Evaluate.hxx`) checks the data of
+the batch, reads the arguments and writes the output and the statuses of
+the points, and calls the primitive of the backend, shared with the
+behaviours (see the [page of the
+behaviours](generic-parallel-behaviour-interface.html)). The invalid
+parameters (status `-6`) are reported before the other checks of the
+batch, and the execution policy is checked by the primitive, after the
+fields, as for the behaviours.
 
 ## Execution policies and statistics
 
